* LT1720 Comparator: 5V supply, 1.65V resistor-divider threshold,
* open-drain-style output with pull-up resistor, input held above threshold
* -> OUT should sit LOW (~0 V)

*-------------------- Supplies --------------------
VCC   VCC   0   DC 5

*-------------------- Threshold divider: 5V * 3.3k/(6.7k+3.3k) = 1.65V ----
R1    VCC   VTH   6.7k
R2    VTH   0     3.3k
CBYP  VTH   0     100n

*-------------------- Input (held above the 1.65V threshold) --------------
VIN   IN    0   DC 3.3

*-------------------- Comparator --------------------
* Pin order: +IN  -IN  V+  V-  OUT
* IN drives the inverting input, threshold on non-inverting input,
* so IN > VTH forces OUT LOW.
XU1   VTH   IN   VCC   0   OUT   LT1720

*-------------------- Open-drain-style pull-up + load --------------------
RPU   VCC   OUT   1k
CL    OUT   0     10p

*-------------------- Supply decoupling --------------------
CVCC  VCC   0     1u

*-------------------- Models --------------------
.include LT1720.sub

*-------------------- Analysis --------------------
.tran 0 1m 0 1u
.meas TRAN vout_dc AVG V(OUT) FROM=800u TO=1m
.meas TRAN vth_chk AVG V(VTH) FROM=800u TO=1m

.end
